# Prisma computes a SHA-256 checksum of each migration.sql's exact bytes and
# compares it against the checksum recorded when that migration was applied.
# On Windows, core.autocrlf can rewrite a migration file's line endings on
# checkout (LF -> CRLF), changing its checksum and making `prisma migrate dev`
# falsely believe an already-applied migration was edited, prompting a
# database reset it doesn't actually need. Keep these files byte-identical
# across platforms.
prisma/migrations/**/migration.sql -text
